fork system call

In parent
— fork returns child
pid
In child process
— fork returns 0

Other system calls
— Wait, returns pid
of an exiting child

int pid;

pid = fork();
if (pid > 0) {
printf (“Parent : child PID = %d”, pid);
pid = wait();
printf (“Parent : child %d exited\n”, pid);
} else{
printf (“In child process”) ;
exit(0);

